{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies","id":980714,"title":"Some mad science-based Legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-03T05:37:01-07:00","id":980714,"title":"Some mad science-based Legacies","content":"Decided to put these two and possibly more together. Basically, as part of Operation Where's The Mad Science, I've been brainstorming some weird science-based Legacies, and I have two so far. <br /> <br /> The first is a Legacy of mages who embrace the &quot;mad scientist&quot; label by taking on the role of supervillains. Why they do this varies widely, but many see themselves as necessary evils, providing humanity with an outlet to rail against or a rival to challenge them. Needless to say, this legacy attracts a number of Beast hangers-on. In universe, this idea has been around in various forms for as long as humanity has had the concept of a villain, but this specific Legacy emerged in the 1960s, after the archetype supervillain had become firmly established. Its founder, the Pathless neurologist Craniac the Undying, continued to be active within the Legacy's community, until she vanished following a confrontation with a particularly nasty Banisher in the Brazilian rainforest. However, given Craniac's obsession with immortality and survival, her closest friends are certain she will one day return in some form. <br /> <br /> As for gameplay, I'm not sure they need any membership restrictions other than ideological ones. I can't see them being path restricted. I'm not sure where they fit into the factions, either. I'd say that the Pentacle and the Free Council both grudgingly tolerate them but the Seers really hate them. Matter makes a good Ruling arcana for them. It's what you use to build volcano lairs and giant robots, after all, and it works as a callback to the Society of Ether. Not sure about Attainments, but I do like the idea of them focusing on making large engineering projects easier. <br /> <br /> The second is a Silver Ladder Legacy of Deist retro-tech utopians, who are basically the Lemurians from Genius ported into Mage. Well, there's also a lot of influence from the Society of Aether and the Mechanomancers from UA. While they aren't Path restricted, it's been estimated that up to half of them are Obrimos. Their Ruling arcana is Matter as well. They have a complicated relationship with the Austere: they both arose from a single ancient parent Legacy of clockworkers, but found different focuses. This connection has become something of a liability, as the brutal methods of the Austere have come under increasing scrutiny in modern times. The legacy, and utopianism in general, also suffered a huge blow during the Lemurian Catastrophe during the turn of the century, in which an attempt to raise an island as a &quot;New Atlantis&quot; went horribly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:46:36-07:00","id":980742,"title":"","content":"The foils fit the Acanthus path fairly well, given the narrative role you've defined for them. The specific trappings of &quot;science&quot; would be rather modern. This almost sounds like a Cult or lesser/Nameless order that has a suite of legacies and practices.<br /> <br /> The Moros path fits your general description of a mad scientist throughout history, i might add, no legacy needed. (That is, they fit their time's closest concept of a mad scientist.) Reviving the dead and making strange animate things out of non-living materials both fit their capacities and predilections. A legacy that lets them keep their creations active in the face of Disbelief would be only particular advantage of a legacy for the concept you describe. An extra arcanum to play with is a pretty distant second to that. That's why it's hard to pick a proper third arcanum. Mind, Time, and Forces are the most obvious competition.<br /> <br /> A mad scientist who makes creepy machine-corpse things in his basement is a pretty stereotypical low-wisdom Free Councillor or Solitaire Moros who chose mechanics as a focus for his work. With the FC Yantra schtick in 2e, that's particularly workable.<br /> <br /> <br /> The second one sounds like you've come up with an Obrimos legacy with Matter primary. Maybe when you flesh them out further it will be easier to see what you intend them to be.<br /> <br /> Not at all clear on what you plan for either of these to actually *do*, honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:12:25-07:00","id":980806,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't really <i>get</i> the entire mad scientist thing. I mean yeah, of course I've seen various examples of it throughout fiction, but I still just don't really <i>get it</i>. What exactly makes a mad scientist a mad scientist? Are they just evil wizards with science trappings? To me mad scientists have always seemed like other types of villains (or heroes sometimes too I guess) that just take the usual trope, add a thin layer of pseudoscience paint, and call it a day. What am I missing here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:14:11-07:00","id":980860,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I always think Girl Genius, which yeah is basically magic with sprockets and old fashioned light bulbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:02:14-07:00","id":980963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=980860#post980860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, I always think Girl Genius, which yeah is basically magic with sprockets and old fashioned light bulbs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was pretty much what I was thinking. I was thinking of a mad scientist Legacy but all I really got from it was a bunch of Legacy ideas that essentially was a completely standard Mage Legacy with a bunch of gears and sprockets randomly thrown in. So is that really all mad scientist stuff is? Wizards (or Mutants/Superheroes/Whatever) with pseudoscience tacked on? I still feel like I have to be missing something. I'm hoping that someone much more familiar with the genre than myself can enlighten me on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:33:19-07:00","id":980985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=980963#post980963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was pretty much what I was thinking. I was thinking of a mad scientist Legacy but all I really got from it was a bunch of Legacy ideas that essentially was a completely standard Mage Legacy with a bunch of gears and sprockets randomly thrown in. So is that really all mad scientist stuff is? Wizards (or Mutants/Superheroes/Whatever) with pseudoscience tacked on? I still feel like I have to be missing something. I'm hoping that someone much more familiar with the genre than myself can enlighten me on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mad science&quot; is when a &quot;scientist&quot; character (almost always a caricature) &quot;crosses lines man was never meant to cross&quot; using &quot;science&quot; (as you noted, almost always pseudo-science).<br /> <br /> The reason you're having problems coming up with Mage flavors of mad science legacies is because Mages already fill most of the same tropes. A Mad Scientist's primary sin is Hubris! A Mad Scientist's primary goal is to push beyond the limits of mortal knowledge and investigate whatever Mystery has grabbed their attention!<br /> <br /> Mad Scientists are the modern equivalent of obsessed mages, so obsessed mages will inevitably be difficult to distinguish from Mad Scientists (this is the biggest narrative failing of the <i>Genius: the Transgression</i> fansplat, it has no room to form its own identity).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MadScientist\" target=\"_blank\">TvTropes page for fun.</a> In the <i>Magic: the Gathering</i> card game most of the &quot;mad scientist&quot; types are Wizards, a rare few are Artificers (most Artificers tend to be more mentally stable).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:37:18-07:00","id":980987,"title":"","content":"As far as I've known, traditionally 'mad science,' which I think is more recently called 'weird science,' to disassociate it from the mentally ill is stuff that crosses some societal boundaries. Sometimes it works, but it's something you shouldn't do, but sometimes it shouldn't work and is just science-fiction which is basically magic using more relatable terminology. Going away from the scientist, sometimes it is stuff that exists but doesn't make sense with our understanding of science.<br /> <br /> In mage, the equivalent would be following a Left-hand path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:40:21-07:00","id":980991,"title":"","content":"There are people in real life I'd be inclined to call actual mad scientists, and that can range from the horrifically hubristic and useless to the possibly doing something awesome in a hubristic way by flouting either convention or conventional ethics. Ramp it up to supernatural levels though and I still think Mage covers it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:14:47-07:00","id":981015,"title":"","content":"Well, we have official term of technognostic Awakened...<br /> <br /> To be more useful with idea - Each Legacy, at the heart, has one large Obsession that is driving it's members and it's sum up in Theory section. So maybe brainstorm some ideas on Technognostic ones?<br /> <br /> I may start:<br /> <br /> <i>Revivers</i> - Moros mages looking for answer when souls move on to afterlife because they want to brought people back to life. ( Yes, it's basically <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oCm_NMU6Phw\" target=\"_blank\">Flatliners</a> movie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <i>Transfers </i>- Truly free Mind can travel between bodies. Let's make this happen! ( Probably Mastigos concentrated on Mind and Matter )<br /> <br /> <i>Soul-Hackers</i> - Your Soul is software, so it can be hacked! ( I do not know if <b>Cloud Infinite</b> Legacy do not stole this idea )<br /> <br /> <i>Evolutionists</i> - Thyrsus - Every species can risen to new hights - let's uncover next perfect beings!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-03-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:48:23-07:00","id":981036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies#post980714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for gameplay, I'm not sure they need any membership restrictions other than ideological ones. I can't see them being path restricted. I'm not sure where they fit into the factions, either. I'd say that the Pentacle and the Free Council both grudgingly tolerate them but the Seers really hate them. Matter makes a good Ruling arcana for them. It's what you use to build volcano lairs and giant robots, after all, and it works as a callback to the Society of Ether. Not sure about Attainments, but I do like the idea of them focusing on making large engineering projects easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest making them Free Council or a Nameless order, the latter route gives you some options with Mystery Cult Initiation as a special merit for them. Might be good to grant them Patient, Good Time Management, and Hobbyist Clique.<br /> <br /> I would suggest doing them as a Matter/Forces Legacy, with some Time thrown in too since they're weirdos anyway. Some spells you might think about for Attainments:<br /> Forces 1 Tune In<br /> Forces 2 Transmission<br /> Matter 1 Craftsman's Eye<br /> Matter 2 Remote Control<br /> Matter 3 Wonderful Machine<br /> Matter 3 Shrink and Grow<br /> Time 3 Acceleration with the Reach effect that cuts extended action times<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:49:00-07:00","id":981037,"title":"","content":"The thing that came to my mind while reading your description, not the super villain part, was a legacy of Mages who work to create imbued items that don't suffer Paradox and more importantly Dissonance. They would seek to do this by manipulating the rules of the Fallen World to accept their magical creations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:17:08-07:00","id":981059,"title":"","content":"I remember years back <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> wrote up a group of Scelesti who deliberately worked with the Nemesis Continuum from Intruders. It was a pretty neat idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:18:53-07:00","id":981063,"title":"","content":"It bears noting that membership in the secret religions that are the Pentacle orders doesn't actually preclude membership in other cults. Certain factions (Wrens, say) should be effectively Cults within the greater orders. Others should cross order lines.<br /> A left-handed faction of scientists that research the division between living and dead by tearing minds and souls from bodies to insert them into other things would certainly qualify as creepy and act like a mad scientist from most the most pulpy of fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:24:56-07:00","id":981157,"title":"","content":"Well, the parts that were helpful were helpful. Can we have a new rule that maybe showing up in people's homebrew threads to say &quot;I don't even understand why you're doing this, I don't get it, please explain it to me again&quot; isn't helpful? I don't enjoy having to defend every single thing I suggest because it doesn't fit some people's vision of the game. I'm not sure what &quot;but what do you want them to do&quot; means, Person Who's Signature Is Not Encouraging. I want them to be a fun and interesting addition to the game. Look, if you don't understand the archetype of the mad scientist, if you don't like it, that's fine, but we get it. <br /> <br /> The whole shadow name/persona thing brings the game close to superhero territory, so I figured I might as well work with that. Plus, that would bring it closer to being The Venture Bros: The Game, which would be AWESOME. <br /> <br /> I've said in another thread that a mad scientist is definitely close to being a wizard with a technological coat of paint, and that's one of the reasons I find them compelling- the divide between actual science and weird science is what makes them a kind of monster, the way Genius explored that was incredible, and I want to include more of that in Mage. <br /> <br /> Basically, for Mage, I'm trying to make it closer to Ascension in that the Mage umbrella. I don't want there to be a hard and fast line between Mage and mad scientist. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I like the idea that the Acanthus legacy (let's actually just call them The Foils) is an older one based on taking the role of the villain, and this one is a newer one based on the more modern archetypes of the supervillain and mad scientist. <br /> <br /> Some of those other ideas are good suggestions for other legacies, but keep in mind that this isn't just a general &quot;mad science in Mage&quot; thread. Both of the Legacies have pretty clear purposes and conceptual origins: the supervillains represent the idea of deliberately embracing the idea of the villain, playing on the whole &quot;persona&quot; mechanic, while the Lemurians are an attempt to both import the Lemurians from Genius by playing on their similarities with the &quot;atlantean utopia&quot; agenda that some mages have, while also providing a counterpart to the austere that uses the clockpunk aesthetic for a different focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-03-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T23:59:18-07:00","id":981300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981157#post981157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while the Lemurians are an attempt to both import the Lemurians from Genius by playing on their similarities with the &quot;atlantean utopia&quot; agenda that some mages have, while also providing a counterpart to the austere that uses the clockpunk aesthetic for a different focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not know Genius so could you eloborate on those - How Lemurians differ from 'Atlantean' Awakened of <b>Mage</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:09:37-07:00","id":981306,"title":"","content":"Lemurians are the main antagonist splat of Genius. They believe that their personal paradigms are either how the world really works or how it should work. They actually did secretly rule the world in the past, but a massive war with the Peerage in the twentieth century that involved large amounts of time travel broke their hold on humanity, and even retroactively erased their control. The Lemurian Y-splats are known as Baramins, and they represent where they believe history and science went wrong. Lemurians generally believe in working towards some sort of utopian future where the Inspired rule the world openly, and their Paradigms are openly accepted and no longer hampered by Havoc. So, basically, the Ladder's goal, except the Lemurians are all mad scientists and are the antagonist faction. And the fact that their mythical lost city is Lemuria rather than Atlantis. I merged the two, making Lemuria be an imperfect attempt at resurrecting Atlantis that went horribly wrong. This plays into some meta subtext- the devs have said that they moved away from Atlantis in 2e because they didn't want to have the game so heavily tied to hoary turn of the century western pseudoscientific gentleman's club occultism, so the Lemurian legacy here represents the Awakened who still hold on to that idea and refuse to leave it in the past. Despite being mad scientists, they're meant to be a very old and traditionalist faction. Their love of clockwork hardens back to their origins in the Renaissance, and is also a reference to Unknown Armies' Mechanomancers. It also differentiates them from the Transhumanist Adepts and the Free Council in general. They're very much ivory tower philopsher-king wannabes who hold into older ideals of science and technology rather than embracing modern technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-04-2016, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:32:58-07:00","id":981314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981306#post981306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, basically, the Ladder's goal, except the Lemurians are all mad scientists and are the antagonist faction. And the fact that their mythical lost city is Lemuria rather than Atlantis. I merged the two, making Lemuria be an imperfect attempt at resurrecting Atlantis that went horribly wrong. This plays into some meta subtext- the devs have said that they moved away from Atlantis in 2e because they didn't want to have the game so heavily tied to hoary turn of the century western pseudoscientific gentleman's club occultism, so the Lemurian legacy here represents the Awakened who still hold on to that idea and refuse to leave it in the past. Despite being mad scientists, they're meant to be a very old and traditionalist faction. Their love of clockwork hardens back to their origins in the Renaissance, and is also a reference to Unknown Armies' Mechanomancers. It also differentiates them from the Transhumanist Adepts and the Free Council in general. They're very much ivory tower philopsher-king wannabes who hold into older ideals of science and technology rather than embracing modern technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, you should more hammer what Legacy should focus, as you are trying to catch to much crows in one hand. ( Maybe splinting them into two or three separated groups? ) Look over <b>Mage </b>2E corebook <i>11th Question</i> write-up, Theory section especially - each and every Legacy in <b>Mage</b> should strife from one rather straightforward dogma of it. It can split and expend a bit from that, but mostly should be specialized. You need also focus on Path, as Path is main 'Legacy transmitter' - Legacy can be 'Order-wide' ( or even two 'Order-wide' ) but most important is Path relation in it.<br /> <br /> You should also contrast them with Dakasha Legacy ( from <b>Legacies: The Sublime</b> ) as those are Theosophiest in Mysterium, believing themselves to hailing from Lemuria. Also, could work contrasting idea with Loyalists of Thule of Hunter, as they are believing in ancient Atlantean Mage-Kings also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-04-2016, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:47:40-07:00","id":981321,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty obvious that they have a clear focus. &quot;Clockpunk and steampunk wannabe philosopher kings who want to resurrect the utopia they believe they lost&quot; is pretty clear. &quot;Should strife from one rather straightforward dogma of it&quot; is not a series of words that I understand. <br /> <br /> There are an Order legacy, for the Silver Ladder, who also have a strong connection to the Obrimos but are not exclusive to them. I believe that's a pretty solid set of qualifications. It's pretty clear how they relate to the Obrimos and the Silver Ladder in terms of philosophy. I don't think legacies should only be path-based, or even predominantly path-based. Having a central theme is what I start with, and I pick a path or legacy from there if it makes sense. <br /> <br /> And those are interesting connections to make, I'll consider mentioning those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:56:56-07:00","id":981325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981321#post981321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty obvious that they have a clear focus. &quot;Clockpunk and steampunk wannabe philosopher kings who want to resurrect the utopia they believe they lost&quot; is pretty clear. &quot;Should strife from one rather straightforward dogma of it&quot; is not a series of words that I understand.<br /> <br /> There are an Order legacy, for the Silver Ladder, who also have a strong connection to the Obrimos but are not exclusive to them. I believe that's a pretty solid set of qualifications. It's pretty clear how they relate to the Obrimos and the Silver Ladder in terms of philosophy. I don't think legacies should only be path-based, or even predominantly path-based. Having a central theme is what I start with, and I pick a path or legacy from there if it makes sense.<br /> <br /> And those are interesting connections to make, I'll consider mentioning those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I mentioned before - Legacies 2E are Path based first, Order second. It's because they work with Attainments and Ruling Arcanum of Legacy. For now, you just made Faction in Silver Ladder Order - cool faction, I must admit, but it's not really Legacy idea, yet.<br /> <br /> Theory section should be about what Legacy want to transform their souls in to - remember, Soul Transformation is Legacies main goal ( in reality, powers it get's to character ).<br /> <br /> Question to hammer those guys is simple - <b>What Arcanum would be most important to them and with what other Arcanum of the Path would it work fine as powers for Legacy?</b> Probably Time could work as Legacy Ruling Arcanum, but I have a problem connecting Prime and Forces to the 'mages wanting to resurrect Atlantis' concept, maybe you have idea on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T01:30:39-07:00","id":981345,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree with Wyrd. The Lemurians have a goal and a vague aesthetic, but they don't really have a theory of their legacy that links those two. Though, the mentioning of the Austere kinda points to some interesting possibilities and you've made allusions to a sort of older-style mechanistic cosmology.<br /> <br /> To contrast, the Daksha have a similiar overall goal and their own aesthetic, but they also have a coherent theory of what they're doing and where their attainments fit into that. Plus, it's quite possible for magi to discard the goals of a legacy and still use the attainments for other purposes, I'm not sure I have much of an idea what the Lemurians would look like if one of them did that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:21:16-07:00","id":981396,"title":"","content":"Well, I haven't worked out the attainment yet, but I've seen some similar Legacies to base it on. So that'll answer that when it's worked out in more detail. Presumably, the Attainment has something to do with magical machinery. And Wyrd, I'm sorry, but it is really hard sometimes for me to read your posts, so I'm sorry if I've missed anything you said or meant. <br /> <br /> I could flesh out their backstory more, but I already have it pretty well outlined. Their ideological forerunners emerged in Renaissance Italy, as a group of early technomages and mad scientists who latched on to the popular notions of cosmology and the spirit of progress. Ironically, while the Free Council currently sees them as hidebound past-dwelling elitists, when the first &quot;clockworkers&quot; emerged they were very much like the Free Council of their era- open-minded and willing to embrace new philosophies and technologies, and seen by their more traditionalist contemporaries as sleeper-loving libertines. It did help that prevailing Renaissance notions about enlightenment and the idealization of the classical era fit in very well with Awakened ideals. They continued to grow in power and influence over the years, and the rapid pace of technological and social development seemed to be proof of their ideals. However, they inevitably started to wane. Decades turned into centuries, and their promises utopia still seemed very much out of reach. Humanity didn't seem to he getting any more enlightened. The clockworkers continued to plan and scheme and gather power and materials. When the clockworkers embraced Theosophy, it was out of desperation more than anything else, a fervent desire to believe that their ideals were still relevant and powerful. This grasp for relevance spurred them to muster all their power and resources and attempt to finally create their new Atlantis- which ended up almost destroying them. While the Great War made many Sleepers question the wonders of science and technology, the Lemurian Crisis made quite a few Awakened in the Pentacle start to doubt their utopian dreams. But the clockworkers survived. They say that after the crisis, the only people left were the mad, and that's why the legacy has the goggles-and-death-rays reputation it has now. That's the thing about mad scientists- they don't give up. No matter how many times they fail, they pick themselves up, sew their limbs back on, and build an even bigger robot. The clockworkers, despite all their setbacks, aren't going anywhere. <br /> <br /> To be perfectly honest, I don't care that 2e made Legacies Path first. I'm still going to handle Legacies on a concept-first basis. Though, I am considering changing it to a set of five legacies, one for each path, each with a different emphasis. Together, they make up the Lemurian &quot;faction&quot;. Hmmmm, maybe a Legacy with a different emphasis and attainment for members of each path? I'd still keep that there are more Obrimos than any other Path in their ranks. I'd say that technically Pathless can join, but the Legacy's obsession with order means that they're rather distrusted. I also had the idea that there was a clockwork legacy for each Pentacle faction, but in modern times only the Lemurians and the Austere are left. <br /> <br /> So, I think there's potential for that from a homebrew standpoint. Create a new type of superlegacy that encompasses a legacy for each path under its umbrella. That could work for the supervillain legacy, as well. <br /> <br /> Let's see:<br /> <br /> For the Lemurians:<br /> Obrimos: Pretty obvious. Pretty much what's been described. <br /> Acanthus: Focusing on the &quot;machinery&quot; of time, and using their affinity for luck against it- using Fate to quash uncertainty. Not sure what their new arcana would be. <br /> Thyrsus: Nature's just one big machine, after all. They'd be focused on seeing patterns within the seeming chaos of life. I'd give them Matter, too. <br /> Mastigos: I dunno, they focus on the machinery of the mind? Their version of the attainment focuses on leading crowds of people and helping groups work in unison. <br /> Moros: Something something alchemy. <br /> <br /> For the mad scientists/supervillains:<br /> Obrimos: Mad engineers <br /> Acanthus: Mad physicists <br /> Mastigos: Mad psychologists/evil masterminds<br /> Thyrsus: Mad biologists <br /> Moros: Mad chemists <br /> <br /> You know, it was surprisingly hard to come up with a concept for each one, so I'm not sure where to go from here. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking Matter for their ruling Arcana, as a Society of Ether callback, with either Prime or Forces. There's no real reason to give them Time. Their focus on clockwork isn't for its time-related aspects. Matter, Forces, and Prime all have clear connections to the idea of a mechanistic cosmos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-04-2016, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:38:37-07:00","id":981399,"title":"","content":"Background is nice, but not very practical on gameplay basis for Legacy creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981396#post981396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I am considering changing it to a set of five legacies, one for each path, each with a different emphasis. Together, they make up the Lemurian &quot;faction&quot;. Hmmmm, maybe a Legacy with a different emphasis and attainment for members of each path?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could work - Alternative Attainments are a thing, and on things like Clavicularius and Bane Ashmedi - you can have offshoots that become their own Legacies on to itself. Lemurians could work as 'collective' of sister Legacies. Problem is you still do not seem to know what they would be really doing in game world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981396#post981396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd still keep that there are more Obrimos than any other Path in their ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Population' is all in particular chronicles / ST fiat territory in the end. You can just write that Obrimos are most numerius part of Lemurian factions, but it does not mean very much on game-to-game basis - players will take Legacy they like/have Attainment powers cool to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981396#post981396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that technically Pathless can join, but the Legacy's obsession with order means that they're rather distrusted. I also had the idea that there was a clockwork legacy for each Pentacle faction, but in modern times only the Lemurians and the Austere are left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good would be too look how different are Lemurians compared to them and how work Austere in 2E. If I remember, Austere worked as Guardians Legacy - reworking them in 2E would highlight what niches are free or needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981396#post981396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking Matter for their ruling Arcana, as a Society of Ether callback, with either Prime or Forces. There's no real reason to give them Time. Their focus on clockwork isn't for its time-related aspects. Matter, Forces, and Prime all have clear connections to the idea of a mechanistic cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Real question is straight forward - <b>W</b><b>hat do you want them to do, on day-to-day basis? </b>They are to create robots and gadgets - Make them Matter based. They are to work as Time Travelers - give them Time Arcanum as Ruling. Attainments and Legacy Ruling Arcanum are there to help they fullfil Legacies self-imposed jobs.<br /> <br /> Mechanics are simple - <b>You just seem to not know what they should do on gameplay level</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-04-2016, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:42:34-07:00","id":981572,"title":"","content":"Of course I don't know what they do on a gameplay level, I haven't worked out the crunch yet. Again, I don't really give a shit about &quot;practical&quot;. The narrative and setting are what's most important for me, and it's standard for me to do that and then work out the mechanics later. I think we're approaching the setting in different ways. Since this is homebrew and I don't have a word count limit, I can write as much backstory as I can think of. I'm not entirely sure what you mean by &quot;you don't know what they should be doing&quot;. If you mean that I haven't worked out an attainment yet, I'm fully aware of that and repeatedly reminding me of it does not accomplish anything. Proposing ideas for an attainment would be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:53:06-07:00","id":981581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981572#post981572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course I don't know what they do on a gameplay level, I haven't worked out the crunch yet. Again, I don't really give a shit about &quot;practical&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a pitty, as 90% of Mage write-ups is 'practical'. Fluff is nice, but to make group, you need mechanics for it just to work in game world. Other than that, it's not really Legacy but philosophical Faction in Order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981572#post981572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely sure what you mean by &quot;you don't know what they should be doing&quot;. If you mean that I haven't worked out an attainment yet, I'm fully aware of that and repeatedly reminding me of it does not accomplish anything. Proposing ideas for an attainment would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that you do not have idea what are they doing in game, what's they shtick. Like, you just literary admited it.<br /> <br /> We cannot make Attainments on guys you do not have idea will do with them. To hammer Attainment you need:<br /> <br /> A. General idea of what Legacy members should <i>do</i> in game world,<br /> and<br /> B. Ruling Arcanum.<br /> <br /> If you do not have any idea on those, maybe look over for fan created 2E Legacies to have a better handle what those groups need - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/924832-wyrd-s-legacies-hub\">here is list of mine</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-04-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:57:42-07:00","id":981585,"title":"","content":"Okay then. They have a backstory, a goal, a philosophy, and an aesthetic. What they &quot;do&quot; is try to create their utopia and recover from their losses, in ways that involve creating clockpunk and steampunk machinery. So, I have the general idea, and I have the ruling arcanum decided. I know they need an attainment. If you want to suggest ideas for an attainment, feel free to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:01:24-07:00","id":981588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981585#post981585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What they &quot;do&quot; is try to create their utopia and recover from their losses, in ways that involve creating clockpunk and steampunk machinery. So, I have the general idea, and I have the ruling arcanum decided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Recreate 'utopia' ( non-existing timeline) will be Time focused group. Making *punk machinery would be Matter.<br /> <br /> Need to choose what is more important to them of two. Can have both if you made them Moros on Time or Acanthus on Matter, but it still be a bit different groups then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:09:08-07:00","id":981594,"title":"","content":"No, sorry. You're getting too hung up on semantics. They don't literally want to travel back in time (which would work, since in 2e &quot;Atlantis&quot;, whatever it was, doesn't correspond to linear time). They have Matter primary because they believe that the entire cosmos can best be understood as an elaborate machine, and the best way to manipulate it is with the creation and use of machinery. I don't think I need to choose one- &quot;makes machines&quot; and &quot;wants a utopia&quot; are too vague to support a legacy on their own. &quot;Believes in a mechanistic cosmos and uses technomagical inventions to work towards an enlightened utopia&quot; seems perfectly workable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:25:50-07:00","id":981605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981594#post981594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, sorry. You're getting too hung up on semantics. They don't literally want to travel back in time (which would work, since in 2e &quot;Atlantis&quot;, whatever it was, doesn't correspond to linear time).</div> </div> </div> </div>'Atlantis' thing doesn't matter if you want to made Time base Legacy Attainments - for example, <i>Cult of the Doomsday Clock</i> is changing local timeline to change it to their need. I can see Legacy that want to pull things from their own 'Atlantis' - but it would be more Free Council, as it would be rather Metropolis than classical Atlantis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981594#post981594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have Matter primary because they believe that the entire cosmos can best be understood as an elaborate machine, and the best way to manipulate it is with the creation and use of machinery. I don't think I need to choose one- &quot;makes machines&quot; and &quot;wants a utopia&quot; are too vague to support a legacy on their own. &quot;Believes in a mechanistic cosmos and uses technomagical inventions to work towards an enlightened utopia&quot; seems perfectly workable.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Believe' is also too vague - literally all Legacies <i>believes</i> in something, to work with Soul Shaping. Core is to get what they <b><i>do</i></b> with it in the game world, what they basic actions is to achieve those beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-04-2016, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:35:12-07:00","id":981613,"title":"","content":"But I don't want to make time their ruling arcana. I'm not sure why you're getting hung up on that. And I'm really tired of the people painting the Free Council as just &quot;the technomages&quot;. I've explained what differentiates the Lemurians from the FC and what makes them a Ladder legacy. <br /> <br /> Okay, and I've described what they do. Their backstory even includes a specific example of a large-scale magical engineering project they attempted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:52:15-07:00","id":981631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981613#post981613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, and I've described what they do. Their backstory even includes a specific example of a large-scale magical engineering project they attempted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have described a vague historical grand endeavor based on an incredibly broadly-defined goal and a very superficial application of skill. The Legacy's teeth are needed for it to talk properly, and those are found in the space between those two endpoints.<br /> <br /> What, apart from &quot;does *punk machinery aesthetics,&quot; gives the Legacy the mundane prerequisites it builds from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:59:46-07:00","id":981639,"title":"","content":"So, what are you asking? What a member of this legacy does as part of their day to day life? What a member of this legacy would do during a session of play? What their utopia would look like? Initiation? Oblations? All are valid questions, and they're ones I'm hoping to eventually cover. Suggestions are welcome, but just reminding me that I don't have those things done yet does not help. I'm aware that I don't have anything near a finished product, but I'm working towards that. I do believe, however, that I have a valid overall concept, and it seemed like Wyrd was saying that I didn't. I think, I've mentioned it's quite hard to parse their posts. <br /> <br /> And does anyone have any thoughts on the supervillain legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:20:18-07:00","id":981651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981639#post981639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what are you asking? What a member of this legacy does as part of their day to day life?</div> </div> </div> </div>The members of the Eleventh Question are magical investigators seeking enlightenment as to the ultimate truth through holistic examination of evidence.<br /> <br /> The Tamers of Fire are heroes and leaders and rabble-rousers attempting to embody the true nature of Fire.<br /> <br /> &quot;Utopians&quot; does not tell us anything about the Mechapunk Legacy's activity and &quot;Builders&quot; does not tell us anything about their end goal. <i>What <u>are</u> they?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think, I've mentioned it's quite hard to parse their posts. </div> </div> </div>English is not his first language and complaining that you can't understand him is substantially less helpful than asking for clarification. This is not difficult to figure out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:26:54-07:00","id":981656,"title":"","content":"Okay, builders and scientists and philosophers attempting to create a perfectly ordered utopia. Does that sum them up? But I think I've covered the overall/big picture stuff, and now it's time to work on specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:34:20-07:00","id":981660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981656#post981656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, builders and scientists and philosophers attempting to create a perfectly ordered utopia.</div> </div> </div> </div>So have fascists, communists and genocidal mad men. How do these people try to do it differently then the above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:54:39-07:00","id":981672,"title":"","content":"Arcanum: Prime and Fate.<br /> <br /> They focus predominately on Imbued and Enhanced Items (their &quot;technology&quot;), meaning Prime. They also wish to make sure the &quot;correct&quot; outcomes happen to achieve their Utopia, hence Fate. I'd think their end goal might be a vast Probability Engine, controlling all those bits of circumstances and ensuring everything obeys The Rules to achieve the Optimum Result possible. A world where everything goes &quot;right&quot; (because their mass magic device arm-wracks probability into choosing their preferred outcomes).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now that I've typed it out, Fate is probably Primary, being core to their goals, while Prime is always useful, but not strictly required.<br /> <hr /><br /> Another &quot;Mad Science&quot; Legacy might leverage Matter and Mind to create artificial intelligent forms. I'd say &quot;lifeforms&quot; but they wouldn't have Life. More, Sentient Robots. Less focus on the AI, more on the robot. Yes, one could argue Forces, but this is more about the machine being able to think, rather than using the medium of electricity, EM, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-04-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:36:59-07:00","id":981785,"title":"","content":"Maybe they attempt to achieve the cosmic engine that generates their vision of utopia by turning themselves into the gears and cogs of the machine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> Wyrdhamster is right, you really have to narrow down how they attempt to accomplish their vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:05:33-07:00","id":981803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981660#post981660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So have fascists, communists and genocidal mad men. How do these people try to do it differently then the above?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooooh, Godwinning! I didn't expect this thread to go there. You might note that I never said that what they were doing was right or even advisable, and the defining historical event I connected them to was a resounding failure for them. <br /> <br /> I still want to stick with Matter, because I feel like Fate or Time makes them closer to being quantum physicists, and I don't want to do that, because I want to connect them to older and outdated understandings of the cosmos. <br /> <br /> Making a giant cosmic engine is a good goal for them, yeah. I think I narrowed it down pretty well for something I just started on when I came up with the idea of Lemuria. I probably should have fleshed it out more in the first post, but basically they tried to create an artificial island, sustained by elaborate clockwork mechanisms located beneath its surface, only to have it go horribly wrong and turn into a Paradox-wracked wasteland. Now, looking at other ways to do that would be fun. Like, for example, a space colony. That would be a good goal for the modern clockworkers. <br /> <br /> As for the supervillains, the &quot;villain&quot; part is more important to them than the science part. They act like mad scientists because the mad scientist is one of the modern world's most potent villainous archetypes, and represents the modern successor of the &quot;evil sorcerer&quot; archetype that past mages who deliberately embraced the role of the villain sought to embody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:58:41-07:00","id":981848,"title":"","content":"So if they're making a giant cosmic engine you have to ask yourself how the individual member of the Legacy contributes to this goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:02:02-07:00","id":981852,"title":"","content":"If you mean ruling arcana and attainment, Matter has obvious implications there, and presumably the attainment has something to do with constructing magical machinery. I've been asking myself that from the beginning, but since I'm not a good mechanics person I haven't come up with any ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:05:11-07:00","id":981854,"title":"","content":"No, I mean, how does an individual member of the legacy seek to help build the machine? How does he work with the other members of his legacy? Attainments aren't a factor yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:15:59-07:00","id":981867,"title":"","content":"That's a valid suggestion, but it's something that I'd already been considering, and at this point just reiterating it isn't really helping. <br /> <br /> Back on track, the endowment for the supervillains is tricky, because I'm sort of split between giving them to obvious &quot;build stuff&quot; endowment, or something more abstract. Like, something representing the villain making a last minute escape so they can return to menace the hero later. There was a fan Entitlement with something like that. Actually, I like the idea of having the supervillains be a newer counterpart to an older and more traditional Acanthus legacy of &quot;foils&quot;, and I'd have that be their Attainment.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Was too harsh on Dubois and went too far in assuming ill intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-04-2016, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:21:05-07:00","id":981870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981867#post981867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I'd really not continue on this with you. That's a valid suggestion, but it's something that I'd already been considering, and I'm not really comfortable continuing on with you given other interactions. </div> </div> </div> </div>Can't stand someone asking the hard questions or poking holes in that logic canoe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:24:12-07:00","id":981872,"title":"","content":"I don't need a white knight <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3953_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3953\" data-vbnamecard=\"3953\">Dwight</a> and frankly I'm annoyed with you because you're not even attempting to pretend to be helpful. I've seen exactly one useful comment out of you so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:24:29-07:00","id":981874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981870#post981870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't stand someone asking the hard questions or poking holes in that logic canoe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I acknowledged that it was a valid question, and I've addressed all of the &quot;hard questions&quot; that have been raised. And it's a homebrew Legacy, not a philosophical debate. There's no logic canoe here. <br /> <br /> Look, can we please...take it down a notch? You don't like me, you don't like my ideas, that's fine. I got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:30:05-07:00","id":981881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981872#post981872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't need a white knight Dwight and frankly I'm annoyed with you because you're not even attempting to pretend to be helpful. I've seen exactly one useful comment out of you so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't say I set out to white knight you, it was more of a opportunity of convenience. <br /> Can you point that one out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:31:13-07:00","id":981882,"title":"","content":"I couldn't resist the rhyme scheme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T00:04:40-07:00","id":981993,"title":"","content":"Returning to idea - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a>, <b>What Lemurians do on day to day basis?</b> It's simple question. If they build mechanisms - they build mechanism. If they predict and plan Utopia - they plan Utopia.<br /> <br /> Then you go level lower - If they build clockpunk mechanisms -<b> What examples of them would be?</b> If you will have a 3 'examples actions' that Legacy members do, you will get your Attainments. <b>If you do not have idea what they could do - Look over Matter Arcanum and just pick spells, one from dots 1 to 5. </b>If they will not work this way, we will get you better suggestions,<br /> <br /> If they take out perfect Utopia - You can choose 5 Time spells.<br /> <br /> As almost all Legacies have two Arcana in Attainments - <b>I just advise you to look over Matter and Time spells, choose 1 per dot that sounds as good idea to have for the Lemurians.</b> Then we will get back to write-up, and hammer it's once more.<br /> <br /> My propositions on Attainments on first look over Time Arcana - for Matter just take those made by the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981289-2e-legacy-thaumatech-engineers\">Thaumatech Engineers</a>.<br /> 1st: Green Light / Red Light<br /> 2nd: Choose the Thread<br /> 3rd: Temporal Summoning - re-fluffed as taking best future version of item<br /> 4th: Rewrite History<br /> 5th: 'Bring the Future' - Custom made Attainment that cast all nearby surrounding to brighter future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T06:36:39-07:00","id":982095,"title":"","content":"So to try honing in on what I'm getting at when I ask what the legacy does let me illustrate the multiplicity of possible approaches. If they're turning themselves into the machine maybe they go with body modification, if they're building the machine maybe it's more straightforward, maybe they're attempting to convert one kind of material into something the machine can use as parts like flesh or souls or smoothies, maybe the machine has actually been created already and what they're really trying to do is turn it on and so they're looking for potential fuel sources. This is why the mission statement of build a mechanistic utopia is too broad, there's nothing to latch onto, no strategy for doing it, nothing that a PC can keep an eye out for or try to bring about in his day to day. Having a grand scheme is great, but you'll never get anywhere if you don't break it down into steps that are actionable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:40:42-07:00","id":982119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981803#post981803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still want to stick with Matter, because I feel like Fate or Time makes them closer to being quantum physicists, and I don't want to do that, because I want to connect them to older and outdated understandings of the cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd argue the entire concept of a Mechanistic Universe is entirely inside Fate's wheel-house. I mean, it is literally the perception and control of the hidden levers that control outcomes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981803#post981803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a giant cosmic engine is a good goal for them, yeah. I think I narrowed it down pretty well for something I just started on when I came up with the idea of Lemuria. I probably should have fleshed it out more in the first post, but basically they tried to create an artificial island, sustained by elaborate clockwork mechanisms located beneath its surface, only to have it go horribly wrong and turn into a Paradox-wracked wasteland. Now, looking at other ways to do that would be fun. Like, for example, a space colony. That would be a good goal for the modern clockworkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking Prime - it is the Arcana of infusing magic into stuff, via Imbued Item. Matter <i>might</i> work, but there is only so far you can go with perfected gears.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980714-some-mad-science-based-legacies?p=981803#post981803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the supervillains, the &quot;villain&quot; part is more important to them than the science part. They act like mad scientists because the mad scientist is one of the modern world's most potent villainous archetypes, and represents the modern successor of the &quot;evil sorcerer&quot; archetype that past mages who deliberately embraced the role of the villain sought to embody.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking Mind and Mastigos when I read this. Deliberately setting themselves up as Adversaries seems like it would require some mind-reading to get just right. Having access to Off-Screen Villain Teleportation in a pinch is just a bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:17:35-07:00","id":982184,"title":"","content":"Mrmdubois and Wyrdhamster have continued working on answering the same question I did. Satchel, too, for that matter.<br /> <br /> Pointing out that you haven't clarified what these guys <i>do</i> isn't something to be defensive about; It is and was no attack. In order to help you flesh your idea, though, out it needs an answer. Pointing out that it's pretty well fleshed-out for a new idea is completely missing the point of the advice you keep getting. That's simply the aspect that is in most need of development and/or clarification, <i>especially</i> if you'd like any help developing the idea further.<br /> <br /> I think what's going on here may be that you think &quot;clockwork aesthetic&quot; tells us something more specific than it does. The dizzying array of things people mean by &quot;clockworks&quot; and &quot;steampunk&quot; mean I can't tell which aspect(s) you mean. If you simply nailed that slippery detail down, you'd be a lot closer to defining their actual activities.<br /> <br /> What they do, though, could be defined by narrative needs, first, which would (sometimes) be possible to reverse engineer into mystical praxes and personal goals. All these things overlap and are what I meant by &quot;what you want them to do&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you mean &quot;clockwork&quot; far more literally than your examples suggest, they could very much be focused on using matter to examine the physical universe and observe how time unfolds, using their measurements and devices to nudge events into existence. (In that version, they might even be a tie-in to the G-M) <br /> Earlier, I suggested an approach where they focus on Anima, where they study the line between inanimate and animate, and switch between them. Others have suggested a wide variety of other approaches. These all fit various notions of the theme so broadly stated. <br /> I'll throw out another idea to play with: A heretical branch of the Tamers. A Tamer of Fire got his hands on the Divine Fire and it burned his mind. Unfortunately, they specialize in touching others' minds with their light. The affected are driven to create but are pushed into madness. <br /> <br /> At any rate, good luck with your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:25:05-07:00","id":991686,"title":"","content":"Here's another seed for a Legacy, starting with their attainment: a Legacy of cyberneticists with an Attainment that allows them to modify human bodies without having to use Life. So, they don't need Life+Matter to attach a cyborg arm, they just need Matter. Their ultimate attainment makes them completely inorganic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T00:32:44-07:00","id":991763,"title":"","content":"Okay, for names, how about<b></b>: The Architects of the Divine Machine and the Society for the Propagation of Doom and Peril?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}